ife","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"asz2Bsfk5vIn6Hh4K4BQeQ","review_id":"_NAr2IttvCV-0bPj5oda4A","date":"2019-02-14T02:36:53","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9466055035591125,"text_excerpt":"I love visiting this brewery. They're in such a prime location (right off of Frenchmen Street) - perfect for spreading the good word of craft beer. This was my 2nd visit - almost a year later from my first, and every beer was different from what I had the first time. They don't really have any flagship beers - they seem to brew whatever interests them and whatever they think people would enjoy. There is something there for everyone, and you can crack open a crowler and go on your way into the Quarter or up Frenchmen Street. They tend to have a large number of beers on tap, so don't be surprised if you need to get a snack from one of their guest food vendors. Here's to many more years!!"},{"business_id":"asz2Bsfk5vIn6Hh4K4BQeQ","review_id":"kz5u7-bCFXKvp-z2KTO6YQ","date":"2018-10-29T20:46:10","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.943958580493927,"text_excerpt":"I really enjoyed Brieux Carre's atmosphere and beers. We came in on a Sunday night and it wasn't crowded at all. I liked the quieter atmosphere since I'm not really the Bourbon Street type, though I'm sure the brewery is full and bustling on busier nights. They have a great back yard with picnic tables and a grill fired up for fresh nachos and other food. I had a four beer flight. One gose and three IPAs: \"It's Pronounced Gose,\" \"Falcon Warrior,\" \"Not the Helicopter, Ya Dummy,\" and \"Brut Scootin' Boogie.\" Their gose is super good, really tart and refreshing on a warm day. Of the IPAs I liked Not the Helicopter the best. It's soft and citrusy with a nice mouthfeel. Overall this may have be..."},{"business_id":"asz2Bsfk5vIn6Hh4K4BQeQ","review_id":"4wnrkimZ3QbwFK_nEvCTYA","date":"2018-01-14T05:34:14","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9381693005561829,"text_excerpt":"Had a quick chance to stop by the brewery while wandering through the city. I am always a fan of a good beer and a place that offers some good different stuff. We had a sour and oatmeal milk stout and both were awesome. They have a ton of beers and you can grab a sampler to try everything else out which means you are bound to find something you like when you roll over. Plus, the location is in a great stop to get a beer or two and be able to wander over somewhere to grab some food. Definitely a brewery worth stopping by when you need to get away from the sugary drinks on Bourbon Street!"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"asz2Bsfk5vIn6Hh4K4BQeQ","photo_id":"YdqB25adBCW0G6WjTMd9rA","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/YdqB25adBCW0G6WjTMd9rA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.902076244354248},{"business_id":"asz2Bsfk5vIn6Hh4K4BQeQ","photo_id":"2MG6tJMtDDWqJMwvRjKiqA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/2MG6tJMtDDWqJMwvRjKiqA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8754159212112427},{"business_id":"asz2Bsfk5vIn6Hh4K4BQeQ","photo_id":"-EyxTPppG_5UI-kVd2VaYw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/-EyxTPppG_5UI-kVd2VaYw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8623338937759399},{"bu